Responsibilities: 
Collected antimicrobial peptide data from the DBAASP database using its API.
Extracted peptide sequences, MIC measurements and bacterial target information.
Cleaned the dataset by removing missing and invalid sequences.
Standardised MIC measurements into µM and calculated pMIC values.
Performed exploratory data analysis on MIC distributions, sequence lengths and unique peptides.
Standardised bacterial names to identify the seven ESKAPEE pathogen groups.
Extracted bacterial species, strain names, Gram classification and target-level information.
Installed and configured CD-HIT for peptide sequence clustering.
Clustered similar peptide sequences using an 80% sequence identity threshold.
Assigned cluster IDs and handled short sequences and singleton groups.
Implemented cluster-based Train-Validation-Test splitting using GroupShuffleSplit.
Verified zero sequence and cluster overlap between datasets.
Extracted Amino Acid Composition (AAC) features (20 dimensions).
Extracted Dipeptide Composition (DPC) features (400 dimensions).
Calculated 8 physicochemical properties using Biopython's ProtParam module.
Installed and configured the pretrained ESM-2 protein language model.
Generated 320-dimensional peptide embeddings using mean pooling.
Saved and integrated embeddings into the training, validation and testing datasets.
Developed baseline regression models using Random Forest, XGBoost and CatBoost.
Performed CatBoost hyperparameter tuning.
Conducted feature ablation experiments to compare different feature combinations.
Investigated target leakage and identified problematic input columns.
Reconstructed leakage-free feature matrices.
Evaluated model performance using MAE, RMSE and R².
Performed feature importance and residual analysis.
